 roofs, siding, windows, and vehicles. Expect\nwind damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* This severe thunderstorm will be near...\nEureka around 1215 AM CDT.\nHillsview around 1235 AM CDT.","instruction":"Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from\nwindows. This storm is capable of producing damaging winds and large\nhail.","response":"Shelter","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SVRABR"],"WMOidentifier":["WUUS53 KABR 090457"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-08-09T04:57:00-00:00...storm...295DEG...19KT...45.77,-99.79"],"windThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxWindGust":["60 MPH"],"hailThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxHailSize":["1.50"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KABR.SV.W.0194.260809T0457Z-260809T0600Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-09T01:00:00-05:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SVR"],"NationalWeatherService":["SVW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7e5fc424cf17d33594c9e8732f4a6e0710b93af2.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-98.8,28.17],[-98.59,28.36],[-98.33,28.45],[-98.33,28.33],[-98.54,28.26],[-98.8,28.07],[-98.8,28.17]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7e5fc424cf17d33594c9e8732f4a6e0710b93af2.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7e5fc424cf17d33594c9e8732f4a6e0710b93af2.001.1","areaDesc":"McMullen, TX","geocode":{"SAME":["048311"],"UGC":["TXC311"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/TXC311"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.02aa56307f6319b87aaa3f9fb059fedf8cb7b3e5.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.02aa56307f6319b87aaa3f9fb059fedf8cb7b3e5.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-08T08:45:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-08T20:13:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-08T20:13:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-08T20:13:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-09T11:15:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-09T15:35:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Corpus Christi TX","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 8 at 8:13PM CDT until August 9 at 3:35PM CDT by NWS Corpus Christi TX","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Texas...\n\nNueces River Near Tilden affecting McMullen County.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring.\n\n* WHERE...Nueces River near Tilden.\n\n* WHEN...Until Sunday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 14.0 feet, Minor lowland flooding occurs, and causes\nsloughs and peripheral channels near the main stream to cut off\nareas of the flood plain, isolating livestock and damaging\nequipment in low areas. Oil field tank batteries and pump jacks\nflood.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:30 PM CDT Saturday the stage was 14.3 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 11.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage\ntonight and fall below action stage by late Monday.\n- Flood stage is 14.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 14.3\nfeet on 05/24/2004.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nEven 6 inches of fast-moving flood water can knock you off your feet\nand a depth of 2 feet will float your car. Never try to walk, swim,\nor drive through such swift water. If you come upon flood waters,\nstop, turn around and go another way.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/crp.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSCRP"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS84 KCRP 090113"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL SUNDAY AFTERNOON"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KCRP.FL.W.0026.000000T0000Z-260809T2035Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-09T15:35:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4012e8981516f4acc66aaf3deb0be40ca8d1a929.001.1,2026-08-07T20:14:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a4006eb38dda81396de878a3ee30877db05dc184.001.1,2026-08-07T08:43:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.422f915b9c8698a61ceeecbb773519636c1559f0.001.1,2026-08-06T20:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c086fb0cb122a2dcaad2d633e16163ca1e2f740.002.1,2026-08-06T08:31:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd351168adba7b138d4b2fd5b257e34ba80d69c4.002.1,2026-08-05T19:53:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15a54361c4ea7596611f53154fbe235d68afe15a.002.1,2026-08-05T10:56:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cfe0cb53516243e5682c1b93f097af5f347ba9d1.002.1,2026-08-04T20:07:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0d85f3f3b48cc9017f55a16e1f1acf4cc74e9f0b.002.1,2026-08-04T15:51:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.52c53adf21b8a3c6773f1bc49de7351006f6e777.002.1,2026-08-04T08:54:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1890e16dec93bc7bd2c40c556f7d88b51dfba240.002.1,2026-08-03T20:13:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c2d46f696ba508a8268a87165a57be61f4e50bb.002.1,2026-08-03T09:17:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a89341f8395f18ac2219ce1a412989c19cd5d270.002.1,2026-08-02T20:24:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.135a0f1988967bd17c986e8c8d19aa89231c27b7.002.1,2026-08-02T14:39:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1b543241930cc661baf187477778f4d98e6501dc.001.1,2026-08-02T08:25:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b